{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Do not defile yourselves.</b> The dagesh in the tet is because the tav of the hitpa'el is absorbed, not a nun of the nif'al binyan. And the proof is the dagesh in the tet is because the tav of the hitpa'el is absorbed, not a nun of the nif'al binyan. And the proof is the dagesh in the mem as is the rule. Now behold, He mentioned all of them, that they defile the soul." "<b>from being vomited out before you.</b> Its meaning: from the pure land — [whether] dead or exiled."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text repeats the phrase 'והעד דגשות הטי״ת להתבלע תי״ו התפעל ולא נו״ן בנין נפעל' twice, a likely dittography; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:46.194476624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}